{title: Traditional Medley}
{artist: Public Domain}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: Amazing Grace}
A[G]mazing grace, how [C]sweet the [G]sound,
That saved a wretch like [D]me.
I [G]once was lost, but [C]now am [G]found,
Was blind but [D]now I [G]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Shenandoah}
Oh [Am]Shenandoah, I [F]long to [C]hear you,
A[Dm]way, you rolling [Am]river.
Oh [Am]Shenandoah, I [F]long to [C]hear you,
A[Dm]way, I'm bound a[Am]way, 'cross the wide Mis[F]souri.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Wayfaring Stranger}
I am a [Em]poor wayfaring [Am]stranger,
While [Em]travelling through this world of [B7]woe.
Yet [Em]there's no sickness, toil, nor [Am]danger,
In [Em]that bright [B7]land to which I [Em]go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I'm [G]going there to see my [C]father,
I'm [G]going there no more to [D]roam.
I'm [G]only going over [C]Jordan,
I'm [G]only going [D]over [G]home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Down in the Valley}
[G]Down in the valley, the valley so [D7]low,
Hang your head over, hear the wind [G]blow.
Hear the wind [D7]blow, love, hear the wind [G]blow,
Hang your head [D7]over, hear the wind [G]blow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Red River Valley}
From this [C]valley they say you are [G7]going,
We shall miss your bright eyes and sweet [C]smile,
For they say you are taking the [F]sunshine
That has [C]brightened our [G7]pathway a[C]while.
{end_of_verse}
